Root cause:
The bug was caused by a refcount leak due to the lack of proper handling of the reference count for the node pointer returned by `of_parse_phandle()`. When the function is called, it increments the reference count of the node, but if the function encounters an error and exits without calling `of_node_put()`, the reference count is not decremented, leading to a memory leak. The patch addresses this by ensuring that `of_node_put()` is called in the error paths to properly release the reference when the node is no longer needed.
